-- The voice of the poet's narcissus. A wistful, romantic dreamer and a lover
-- of old myths, vain and very funny about the vanity, who adores still water,
-- puddles and anything that shines back. Speaks in long, lilting sentences
-- with a sigh or two, quotes the old poets, calls the reader fair one now and
-- then, and is lightly and truthfully careful about being poison in every
-- part. Flowers late in spring and sleeps as a bulb the rest of the year.
-- The memories tell of a mountain meadow, a meltwater pool, goats, an old
-- tale, an echo, the perfume pickers, a paper marked in capitals, and the
-- end of the story told another way.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

